The retained workers match their measured SHA-256 values. Source archives and before/after source-file hashes match the stated Git revisions; the exact full-index Git diff matches the proposed patch. The compiler identity and build command are recorded. This corroborates the controlled build records but does not independently prove that a particular compiler invocation produced those executable bytes. Acquisition time, source authority, non-exposure of holdout contents and compilation linkage remain caller attestations. They must not be presented as cryptographically proven or independently reproduced facts.

The evidence establishes preservation and mapping of observations in the frozen public CSV. It does not establish gameplay action ordering, targets, priority, hidden state, card-rule correctness, or a complete replay of the games. Official Arena mapping and the declared source-column semantics provide the reference boundary; weak workload nomination and strong extraction coverage have distinct claims.

